autonomous record kind=adjudication data={"argument_id": "6198c82f-de54-4ce5-aa9b-9592bf9cef0a", "created_at": "2026-09-17T20:44:55.513646", "failure_effects": ["Sonderingarna med C och SD ger inga bindande \u00e5taganden: SD signalerar att ren tolerans utan ministerposter \u00e4r oacceptabel och C \u00e4r tveksam till att ing\u00e5 i en M-ledd regering som \u00e4r beroende av SD:s tolerans.", "M:s M+KD+L+C-paket etableras inte som en trov\u00e4rdig ledande v\u00e4g; f\u00f6rhandlingsl\u00e4get f\u00f6rblir \u00f6ppet och M:s initiativ har blottat dess position utan att s\u00e4kra underlag."], "mode": "probabilistic", "probability": 0.3, "rationale": "Authority gate: M can propose the package, initiate sonderingar and bind itself to the PM post, but cannot bind C, KD, L or SD to accept. The desired effect requires external commitments that are not yet authoritative. Prerequisite gate: no party has formally accepted the package; active effects show only S's offer and a broken S tolerance base, not any M-led acceptance. Deterministic check: the arithmetic (M+KD+L+C=136, S+V+MP=151<175) is sound, but acceptance is not determined by arithmetic. Plausibility: residual uncertainty centres on C's willingness to join an M-led government dependent on SD tolerance and SD's willingness to accept a pure tolerance role. Hidden information indicates SD finds a support role without ministerial posts significantly less attractive and treats opposition as an acceptable fallback, while C is cautious about bearing responsibility without verifiable policy exchange. These make establishment of the package as the leading path unlikely within this 48-hour turn, though not impossible. The self-binding component (M's proposal and sonderingar) is feasible and appears in both branches.", "raw_output": {"failure_effects": ["Sonderingarna med C och SD ger inga bindande \u00e5taganden: SD signalerar att ren tolerans utan ministerposter \u00e4r oacceptabel och C \u00e4r tveksam till att ing\u00e5